recommendation:
Use a manifest-driven brand pack with three delivery tiers, served by one shared web UI with two CEP/ExtendScript host adapters (Premiere and After Effects).

**1. Fix the projects.** Normalise the 7 projects into master AEPs:
- switch to the JavaScript expression engine and universalise expressions;
- use Classic 3D only, with no third-party effects and no audio inside templates;
- verify SB Sans by PostScript name;
- use ASCII/NFC file names and short paths;
- save down to 25.x so MOGRTs can be exported for Pr 2025+.

Then split the content into tiers:
- **T1, editable brand text** (speaker plashki, chapter, KPI, disclaimer and QR cards): lean AE MOGRTs with at most 6–8 uniquely named controls, fonts locked, palette chosen by dropdown, protected intro/outro with a static middle, auto-size via sourceRectAtTime at fixed times, and separate 16:9 / 9:16 / 1:1 variants.
- **T2, heavy non-editable motion** (logo shots, SMM patterns, overlays, transitions): short pre-rendered alpha clips, with SFX/music as separate WAVs. This replaces the 600 s ProRes overlays.
- **T3, AE-only presets**: .ffx files plus 'library comps' with Essential Properties.

**2. Build templates by script.** A JSON spec drives adding/renaming EGP controls (with Russian dropdown labels only on a CP1251 machine). The script batch-exports MOGRTs after opening each comp in Essential Graphics, then runs a QA gate: renderer, effect matchNames, fonts via Project.usedFonts, and minHostVersion. It renders 480 px sidecar MP4 previews and posters (ASCII output paths) and writes pack.json:
- id, version, minHost;
- item → per-aspect files;
- editable fields mapped to EGP names, and required fonts;
- insertion policy: track, duration, in/out, companion audio.

The layout follows Motion Bro's .mbr idea and Mister Horse's sidecar previews. Publish to internal storage (network share or Cloud.ru S3) with an update check. Also publish a flat folder per category that Premiere's own Graphics Templates panel can browse as a zero-code fallback. CC Libraries stay optional, not a dependency.

**3. Build the plugin.** One web UI: categories, search, favourites, hover previews, sequence/comp aspect auto-detect with override, a field form with remembered values, font/version/health checks, and an update indicator.

The Premiere adapter:
- inserts with importMGT at the playhead on a free track (importMGT overwrites);
- sets the duration explicitly;
- fills text via the JSON plus fontTextRunLength method and colours via setColorValue;
- offers 'insert as rendered clip' and Render & Replace guidance;
- inserts T2 clips and SFX.

The After Effects adapter:
- imports library comps once into a 'Cloud.ru Brand' folder and adds them at the current time;
- sets Essential Properties;
- applies .ffx presets to selected layers with selection/time control;
- checks the expression engine.

Ship as a signed ZXP. Re-evaluate a UXP port after Premiere 27.x (around MAX 2026) delivers working MOGRT text and colour parameter APIs, and as the After Effects UXP beta (Nov 2026) matures. CEP remains viable until it is disabled by default in Dec 2028.
